BUILD_ONLY: ghcr.io/mll-lab-nu/eai-robotangle:<images/robotangle/VERSION> is never public (docs/PROTOCOL.md §2.4, D5).
The maintainers keep it as a non-public organisation package (visibility internal, org members only): 0.2.19 is pushed
(sha256:66b8b157d350d28e43e0c43dbc9bd196a6d20a2e12b20fae57055bdeeb639590). Eval hosts pull it with an org login, or build it
locally under that tag from the pinned HF dataset below; Harbor finds it in the local Docker image store.

Why
  The image contains Genesis AI's Nyx renderer (RoboTangle's RGB observations and replay videos), installed from binary
  wheels on PyPI (gs-nyx) that carry no licence metadata. This is an internal release: every evaluation host builds the
  image locally, and maintainers may keep a private organisation package for internal runners. The rest is Genesis 1.2.1 (Apache-2.0), libuipc (Apache-2.0) built with the determinism patches of the
  release tree, PyTorch (BSD), the pinned pip locks of the release tree, the ALOHA 2 model (MuJoCo Menagerie, BSD-3-Clause)
  and the Robotiq 2F-85 model (MuJoCo Menagerie).

What the image is built from
  - images/robotangle/Dockerfile: images/topogym/Dockerfile of the release commit, UIPC_WHEEL defaulting to prebuilt, plus
    a last stage with every task's frozen instance (/opt/robotangle/instances/<base>/) and stage_instance.py.
  - The build context, prepared by scripts/robotangle/fetch_image_context.sh in images/robotangle/context/ (git-ignored)
    from the private Hugging Face dataset eai-v2-internal/robotangle-assets at the revision pinned in
    scripts/robotangle/assets.json, every file checked against its sha256 there:
      image/release-2dafa5f2b.tar.gz   the release tree (scripts/robotangle/release.json `release_commit`, dev/jianwen
                                       2dafa5f2b): `git archive` of the paths images/topogym/Dockerfile copies;
      image/uipc-prebuilt/             the audited libuipc wheel and its uipc-build.json (sha256 39781d19…, the wheel every
                                       lab evidence image installed; nvcc output is not bit-reproducible, so a wheel
                                       compiled on your host never matches the binding);
      instances/                       every task's frozen instance (instance.json + instance_assets/).
    Access: a member of eai-v2-internal, `hf auth login` (or HF_TOKEN in the environment; never printed).

Host
  blanket_flatten: on a GPU other than the one its frozen PBD states were prepared on (an RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell), the
  task generates the birth state from the recipe frozen in the instance. It caches the state inside the container
  ($TOPOGYM_INITIAL_STATE_CACHE, default /opt/rcb-cache), so a fresh container generates it again. Standard mode
  generates in the sim startup (5-9 min for very_easy, on the agent's clock). Generated states are not oracle-validated
  (docs/benchmarks/robotangle.md, GPU portability). The other families run on any supported GPU.
  Linux x86_64 (not WSL: Nyx needs the NVIDIA Vulkan driver inside the container), an NVIDIA GPU with driver >= 580, Docker
  with BuildKit (default `docker` driver) and the NVIDIA Container Toolkit with the `nvidia` runtime registered (the task
  compose files use `runtime: nvidia` with NVIDIA_DRIVER_CAPABILITIES=all for Vulkan). Exactly one GPU per container (two
  visible GPUs crash Nyx). Build: about 25 GB of free disk (11.3 GB image plus BuildKit cache); network access to docker.io,
  pypi.org, download.pytorch.org and dl.polyhaven.org (the CC0 studio HDRI). Running needs no network. Read access to the HF
  dataset is needed (above).

Build (from the repository root)
  scripts/robotangle/fetch_image_context.sh [<download dir>]
  docker build -f images/robotangle/Dockerfile -t ghcr.io/mll-lab-nu/eai-robotangle:$(cat images/robotangle/VERSION) images/robotangle/context
  (scripts/build_images.sh builds it from images/robotangle/BUILD_CONTEXT once the context exists and skips it otherwise.)
  Optional, faster scene builds: images/topogym/warm_cache.sh of the context fills the kernel caches on a GPU host.

Check a build: the image must install exactly the runtime every task is bound to
  docker run --rm ghcr.io/mll-lab-nu/eai-robotangle:$(cat images/robotangle/VERSION) python -c 'import json; from topogym.simulator.frozen_binding import installed_runtime; print(json.dumps(installed_runtime(), sort_keys=True))' > /tmp/robotangle_runtime.json
  python3 -c 'import json, sys; sys.exit(0 if json.load(open("/tmp/robotangle_runtime.json")) == json.load(open("scripts/robotangle/release.json"))["runtime"] else "image differs from the tasks runtime binding: do not run")'
  Every session checks it again at start (`runtime_binding_ok` in reward.json) and refuses a different runtime.
